  "education": {
    "market_education": {
      "summary_en": "Markets shifted into risk-off territory on May 12, 2026, with the NASDAQ falling 1.3% as investors rotated away from growth and technology names amid broader macro uncertainty. Risk-off moves are typically triggered by a combination of factors \u2014 rising bond yields, hawkish Fed signals, geopolitical flare-ups, or disappointing economic data \u2014 that make the reward-to-risk ratio on equities less attractive. The broad-based selling across indices suggests institutional players are reducing exposure rather than targeting a single sector.",
