    "daily_lesson": {
      "term": "Risk-Off",
      "explanation_en": "A 'risk-off' environment is when investors broadly sell higher-risk assets like growth stocks and move into safer havens such as government bonds, gold, or cash. It signals that market participants are more focused on protecting capital than chasing returns. On risk-off days, even fundamentally solid stocks can drop simply because the prevailing mood is fearful or uncertain.",
